        "original_id": "a7a80d84-cec0-580d-a093-a6f1b943b2ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Javier Frana, Thomaz Koch, Patricia Tarabini, Sandra Cecchini, Laura Garrone\n- Organizations: ESPN Latin America\n- Events: French Open, Wimbledon, U.S. National Championships, 1995 Styrian Open – Doubles\n- Places: Argentina, Brazil, Porto Alegre\n- Roles: tennis player, tennis commentator\n\nFacts:\n- Thomaz Koch was born on May 11, 1945, in Porto Alegre, Brazil.\n- Javier Frana was born on December 25, 1966.\n- Thomaz Koch is a left-handed former tennis player from Brazil who reached the quarterfinals at the French Open, Wimbledon, and the U.S. National Championships.\n- Javier Frana is a former tennis player from Argentina and a current tennis commentator for ESPN Latin America.\n- Patricia Tarabini and Javier Frana won the mixed doubles title at the 1996 French Open.\n- Sandra Cecchini and Patricia Tarabini were the defending champions for the 1995 Styrian Open doubles event, but only Sandra Cecchini competed that year, partnering Laura Garrone.",
